  "bookId": "2SA",
  "reference": "2 Samuel 16",
  "verseCount": 23,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "16",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "2SA 16"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "16",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When David had passed a little beyond the summit, Ziba the servant of Mephibosheth met him, with a couple of asses saddled, bearing two hundred loaves of bread, a hundred bunches of raisins, a hundred of summer fruits, and a skin of wine. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And the king said to Ziba, “Why have you brought these?” Ziba answered, “The asses are for the king's household to ride on, the bread and summer fruit for the young men to eat, and the wine for those who faint in the wilderness to drink.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And the king said, “And where is your master's son?” Ziba said to the king, “Behold, he remains in Jerusalem; for he said, ‘Today the house of Israel will give me back the kingdom of my father.’ ” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then the king said to Ziba, “Behold, all that belonged to Mephibosheth is now yours.” And Ziba said, “I do obeisance; let me ever find favor in your sight, my lord the king.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.4"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When King David came to Bahurim, there came out a man of the family of the house of Saul, whose name was Shime-i, the son of Gera; and as he came he cursed continually. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And he threw stones at David, and at all the servants of King David; and all the people and all the mighty men were on his right hand and on his left. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And Shime-i said as he cursed, “Begone, begone, you man of blood, you worthless fellow! ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " has avenged upon you all the blood of the house of Saul, in whose place you have reigned; and the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " has given the kingdom into the hand of your son Absalom. See, your ruin is on you; for you are a man of blood.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.8"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then Abishai the son of Zeruiah said to the king, “Why should this dead dog curse my lord the king? Let me go over and take off his head.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But the king said, “What have I to do with you, you sons of Zeruiah? If he is cursing because the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " has said to him, ‘Curse David,’ who then shall say, ‘Why have you done so?’ ” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And David said to Abishai and to all his servants, “Behold, my own son seeks my life; how much more now may this Benjaminite! Let him alone, and let him curse; for the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " has bidden him. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "It may be that the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " will look upon my affliction,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16.12",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Gk Vg: Heb",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "iniquity",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " and that the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " will repay me with good for this cursing of me today.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So David and his men went on the road, while Shime-i went along on the hillside opposite him and cursed as he went, and threw stones at him and flung dust. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And the king, and all the people who were with him, arrived weary at the Jordan;",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16.14",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Gk: Heb lacks",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "at the Jordan",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " and there he refreshed himself.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.14"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Now Absalom and all the people, the men of Israel, came to Jerusalem, and Ahithophel with him. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And when Hushai the Archite, David's friend, came to Absalom, Hushai said to Absalom, “Long live the king! Long live the king!” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And Absalom said to Hushai, “Is this your loyalty to your friend? Why did you not go with your friend?” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And Hushai said to Absalom, “No; for whom the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " and this people and all the men of Israel have chosen, his I will be, and with him I will remain. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "And again, whom should I serve? Should it not be his son? As I have served your father, so I will serve you.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.19"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then Absalom said to Ahithophel, “Give your counsel; what shall we do?” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Ahithophel said to Absalom, “Go in to your father's concubines, whom he has left to keep the house; and all Israel will hear that you have made yourself odious to your father, and the hands of all who are with you will be strengthened.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So they pitched a tent for Absalom upon the roof; and Absalom went in to his father's concubines in the sight of all Israel. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "2SA 16:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Now in those days the counsel which Ahithophel gave was as if one consulted the oracle",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16.23",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Heb",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "word",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " of God; so was all the counsel of Ahithophel esteemed, both by David and by Absalom.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "2SA.16.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "2SA.16.23"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
